:::



**What I decided.** 8 tracts do not have a computable change in poverty rate. In these cases, the population used to calculate the rate is zero or missing, so the calculation can become 0/0. That is undefined; it does not mean that the poverty rate is 0%.

These are mostly places with very few or no residents, such as industrial areas, parks, or the airport. I did not change these values to zero because that would give them a meaning that the data do not support.

Instead, I left them out of the statistical test and showed them as “No data” on the maps.

### Step 5: Reliability table


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
reliability_table <- poverty_tested %>%
  filter(!is.na(cv_2013_2017)) %>%
  arrange(desc(cv_2013_2017)) %>%
  slice_head(n = 20) %>%
  mutate(
    NAME = str_remove(NAME, ", Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania"),

    dot_10 = case_when(
      reliability_2006_2010 == "Reliable"          ~ "🟢",
      reliability_2006_2010 == "Somewhat reliable" ~ "🟡",
      reliability_2006_2010 == "Unreliable"        ~ "🔴",
      TRUE                                         ~ "—"
    ),
    dot_17 = case_when(
      reliability_2013_2017 == "Reliable"          ~ "🟢",
      reliability_2013_2017 == "Somewhat reliable" ~ "🟡",
      reliability_2013_2017 == "Unreliable"        ~ "🔴",
      TRUE                                         ~ "—"
    )
  ) %>%
  select(
    NAME,
    poverty_rate_2006_2010, poverty_rate_moe_2006_2010, cv_2006_2010, dot_10,
    poverty_rate_2013_2017, poverty_rate_moe_2013_2017, cv_2013_2017, dot_17
  )

reliability_table %>%
  gt() %>%
  fmt_number(columns = -c(NAME, dot_10, dot_17), decimals = 1) %>%
  tab_spanner(
    label = "ACS 2006–2010",
    columns = c(poverty_rate_2006_2010, poverty_rate_moe_2006_2010, cv_2006_2010, dot_10)
  ) %>%
  tab_spanner(
    label = "ACS 2013–2017",
    columns = c(poverty_rate_2013_2017, poverty_rate_moe_2013_2017, cv_2013_2017, dot_17)
  ) %>%
  cols_label(
    NAME = "Census Tract",
    poverty_rate_2006_2010 = "Rate (%)",
    poverty_rate_moe_2006_2010 = "MOE (±pp)",
    cv_2006_2010 = "CV (%)",
    dot_10 = "",
    poverty_rate_2013_2017 = "Rate (%)",
    poverty_rate_moe_2013_2017 = "MOE (±pp)",
    cv_2013_2017 = "CV (%)",
    dot_17 = ""
  ) %>%
  cols_align(align = "center", columns = c(dot_10, dot_17)) %>%
  tab_header(
    title = "Reliability of Tract-Level Poverty Rates",
    subtitle = paste0("The 20 least reliable tracts in 2013–2017 (of ", n_tract, " Philadelphia tracts)")
  ) %>%
  tab_source_note(
    "🟢 CV < 12% reliable; 🟡 CV 12–40% somewhat reliable; 🔴 CV > 40% unreliable (thresholds from Jurjevich et al., 2018). CV = (MOE / 1.645) / rate × 100."
  )
