In 2006–2010, 3% of tracts have a reliable poverty rate and 11% are unreliable. In 2013–2017 the figures are 5% and 6%. This means that a fairly large share of the tract-level estimates have some uncertainty even before comparing the two periods. When we compare the two periods, the uncertainty becomes larger because the errors from both estimates have to be taken into account.

### Step 6: Error bars for the change

The article's headline claims are about the *largest* increases, so I plot the 20 tracts with the biggest estimated increase in poverty, with their 90% margins of error.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
top20 <- poverty_tested %>%
  filter(!is.na(change_rate), !is.na(moe_diff)) %>%
  mutate(NAME = str_remove(NAME, ", Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania")) %>%
  slice_max(change_rate, n = 20, with_ties = FALSE)
bottom20  <- poverty_tested %>%
  filter(!is.na(change_rate), !is.na(moe_diff)) %>%
  mutate(NAME = str_remove(NAME, ", Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania")) %>%
  slice_min(change_rate, n = 20, with_ties = FALSE)

all_error <- rbind(top20,bottom20)

T_n_top_sig   <- sum(top20$significant)
T_med_moe_top <- round(median(top20$moe_diff), 1)
T_min_top     <- round(min(top20$change_rate), 1)
T_max_top     <- round(max(top20$change_rate), 1)

B_n_top_sig   <- sum(bottom20$significant)
B_med_moe_top <- round(median(bottom20$moe_diff), 1)
B_min_top     <- round(min(bottom20$change_rate), 1)
B_max_top     <- round(max(bottom20$change_rate), 1)

ggplot(all_error, aes(x = change_rate, y = reorder(NAME, change_rate), color = direction)) +
  geom_pointrange(aes(xmin = change_rate - moe_diff, xmax = change_rate + moe_diff)) +
  geom_vline(xintercept = 0, linetype = "dashed") +
  scale_color_manual(
    values = c(
      "Significant increase" = "#de2d26",
      "Not significant"      = "grey45"
    )
  ) +
  labs(
  title = "Largest Increases and Decreases in Poverty Rate",
  subtitle = "Philadelphia census tracts, 2006–2010 to 2013–2017. Bars show the 90% margin of error",
    x = "Change in poverty rate (percentage points)",
    y = NULL,
    color = NULL,
    caption = "Source: ACS 5-year estimates (B07012). Top 20 tracts by estimated change."
  ) +
  theme_minimal() +
  theme(legend.position = "bottom")
```

