The 20 largest estimated increases range from 14.9 to 35 percentage points. But their margins of error are large: the median is about ±14.4 points. Only 16 of the 20 have a bar that stays clear of zero. This is important because the largest estimated changes are not necessarily the most reliable ones. When there are many tracts and each estimate has some sampling error, some of the biggest changes can happen partly because of that error.

The 20 Bottom estimated increases range from -78.7 to -14.8 percentage points. And all of their change in proverty rate is not significant.

